      "id": "s02",
      "type": "SCAN_VS_SEEK",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Ask for the orders belonging to one product, and SQLite reads every row and checks each one, because reading everything is the only option available. Six rows here, so nobody cares. Six million and you would care enormously. An index gives the engine a second option: go straight to the answer.",
      "data": {
        "scanVsSeek": {
          "caption": "the same question, asked two ways",
          "premise": "Six orders on disk. You want the ones for product 1.",
          "scanLabel": "SCAN orders",
          "seekLabel": "SEARCH orders USING INDEX",
          "targetIndex": 4,
          "rows": [
            {
